+# GOAL — block 28: the map of memory — where each of the four laws keeps its plane, located numerically against the proved regions, with the healing bound and the influence bound as exact corollaries (2026-09-16)
+
+**Directive.** Owner 2026-09-16: keep running the campaign twelve more hours. After blocks 25–27 the campaign holds proved regions for all four laws (static/formation × six-axis/sphere) but no location of the actual transitions: six-axis static orders for `p ≥ 216 m` (block 17) and is unique for small `p` (block 03); six-axis formation orders for `p ≥ 285718` at `(p, 1, 2)` (block 25) and is unique for `3c < 1`, i.e. `p ≤ 3.7` at `(p, 1, 2)` (block 08); sphere static orders for `β > 76/100` (blocks 19, 22) and is unique for `β < √3/6` (block 21); sphere formation is unique for `β < 1/√3` (block 27) and loses its plane at every `β` tried (block 26). The decision record needs the actual numbers: which reading keeps memory at what strength of preference.
+
+**Exact target (claim type `bounded_theorem`; trace class `frontier_discovery` for the map).**
+- T1 (block 08's criterion at `(p, 1, 2)`, exact): the total-variation sensitivity `c(p)` of the six-axis conditional to one predecessor satisfies `3c < 1` at `p = 37/10` and `3c > 1` at `p = 38/10` (exact rationals), so block 08's uniqueness region on this line ends between; block 25's condition `ε ≤ 7/10⁶` begins at `p = 285718`.
+- T2 (healing): for the noisy majority automaton at noise `ε`, an island of ones at level `0` with coordinate maxima `M_i`, `D = M_1 + M_2 + M_3`, has died by level `D + 1` unless a noise site lies in a space-time region of at most `16(D + 1)³` sites; so `P(the island survives) ≤ 16(D + 1)³ ε`. (Block 12's eroder bound re-proved in two lines; the coupling of the noisy and noiseless evolutions on the noise-free region.)
+- T3 (influence): for the sphere formation law, the influence of one initial record at `x_0` on the record at `x` of level `t` (the per-site coupled distance when the two initial planes differ at `x_0` only) is at most `2(√3β)^t p_t(x − x_0)`, `p_t` the level walk's law; it is confined to the forward cone and, for `β < 1/√3`, decays exponentially in `t` on top of the directed heat kernel.
+- Executed (the map, not proved): the six-axis formation law at `(p, 1, 2)` scanned in `p` on `128²` and `256²` planes (memory of the aligned plane over `4000`–`8000` levels): the strength above which the plane is kept; the six-axis static law on `16³` and `24³` by heat-bath sweeps from aligned and random starts: the strength above which a majority value persists; the sphere static law on `16³`, `24³`: `|m|` against `β`, against `76/100` and `√3/6`; the sphere formation law: block 26. The map placed against the proved regions.
+
+**Falsifiers.** `3c(37/10) ≥ 1` or `3c(38/10) ≤ 1`; an island surviving the noiseless rule beyond `D + 1`; a region count above `16(D+1)³`; an influence exceeding `2(√3β)^t p_t`; for the map: a plane kept below the located strength on a larger plane or longer run, or lost above it.
+
+**Lens pass.** *"Numerics again."* The theorems are small and exact; the map is what the decision record lacks and it is labelled executed. *"Finite-size effects and first-order hysteresis for the static six-axis law."* Two sizes and two starts are run; the located strengths are brackets, not digits. *"The static sphere law is the classical Heisenberg model."* Yes; its transition is known in the literature; here it is re-measured and named as reference only. *"Names."* Only in the allowed sections.
+
+**Forbidden phrases:** the standing list plus "has no ordered phase", "does not order", "converge", "critical", "certified", "phase transition".
