+
+**Deliverables (branch `physics-loop/admissibility-induced-law-block28-map-of-memory-four-laws-located-healing-influence-20260916`, independent PR against `main` at `6dda46fc1a`; parent on `main`: block 01):** the note `docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_MAP_OF_MEMORY_WHERE_EACH_OF_THE_FOUR_LAWS_KEEPS_ITS_PLANE_LOCATED_AGAINST_THE_PROVED_REGIONS_WITH_THE_HEALING_AND_INFLUENCE_BOUNDS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-16.md`; the runner `scripts/admissibility_rule_map_of_memory_four_laws_transitions_located_against_proved_regions_healing_and_influence_bounds_2026_09_16.py` (14 checks, 8 mutations, exact, seven seconds); the pinned cache; the controls (`specs/supervisor_control_block28_exact.py`, `..._scan_formation_sixaxis.py`, `..._scan_static_sixaxis.py`, `..._scan_static_sphere.py`) and the refuting pass (`specs/supervisor_control_block28_refuter.py`) with outputs; `GOAL_block28.md`; `CHECKER_block28_findings.md`; this record. Blocks 06–27 remain open as PRs #8034, #8035, #8138–#8142, #8146–#8158, #8168, #8170, #8171.
+
+**Why this block.** The twelve-hour continuation after blocks 26–27: the campaign held proved regions for all four laws (weak-preference forgetting: 03, 08, 21, 27; strong-preference memory: 17, 22, 25; the sphere formation runs: 26) but no located strengths. The decision record needs the numbers: which reading and which menu keep memory at what strength.
+
+## Result, in one paragraph
+Exact: at `(p, 1, 2)` block 08's criterion `3c < 1` holds at `p = 37/10` and fails at `19/5`, and block 25's condition holds from `p = 285718` (T1); for the noisy majority automaton an island with `D = M_1 + M_2 + M_3` is empty at level `D + 1` under the noiseless rule and, with noise `ε`, has a one in its forward cone at level `D + 1` with probability at most `18(D + 1)³ ε` — the healing bound (T2; block 12's eroder re-proved, a coupling on the noise-free region, the region counted: at most `(D+1)(6D+5)(6D+4)/2`); under the sphere formation law one changed initial record influences the record at level `t` and displacement `y` by at most `2(√3β)^t p_t(y)` (T3). Executed, not proved: the six-axis formation law at `(p, 1, 2)` keeps its aligned plane from a strength between `10.5` and `11` (`128²` and `256²` planes, `4000`–`8000` levels; from a random start the majority grows from `p ≈ 11`); the six-axis static law keeps a majority value from a strength between `3.6` and `3.7` (`16³`, `24³`, `32³`, aligned and random starts, heat bath and single-site proposals); the sphere static law keeps a magnetization from `β` between `0.66` and `0.72` (`16³`, `24³`, both starts; the literature's `0.693` inside); the sphere formation law never (block 26). Against the proved regions: block 17's `432` is a hundred times the static strength, block 25's `285718` twenty-five thousand times the formation strength, block 22's `0.76` within a tenth of the sphere's; block 08's `3.7` sits, by coincidence of this line, where the static law's strength lies. **The static reading keeps memory at about a third of the preference the formation reading needs on the six-axis menu; on the sphere menu only the static reading keeps it.**
+
